course: dictionary
lesson: 3105
title: A name that became a word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Albert Einstein was a famous scientist who studied light, time, gravity and energy. People loved his ideas so much that his name became a word. «You don't have to be an Einstein to see that» means the answer is easy to see, so you do not need to be a genius.
explain: When someone is very clever, we can call them an Einstein. But the tone matters. «Nice one, Einstein!» said after an obvious mistake is sarcastic: the speaker means the opposite of praise. Look at the words around the name to decide whether it is kind or a joke.
explain: «No Einstein» is a joke that means not clever, even though Albert Einstein was very clever. Use context clues: if the sentence is about something easy, the word is praise; if it is about a silly mistake, the word is a joke.
fact: Einstein is a proper noun, so it starts with a capital letter when it is a name.
fact: An Einstein (informal, often joking) means a very clever person.
fact: Albert Einstein's famous idea is written as E = mc².
fact: Einstein did not fail maths. «Einstein did not fail maths; he was very good at it as a boy.»
fact: When it is said sarcastically, «Nice one, Einstein!» means someone has made a silly mistake.
exercise: «You don't have to be an Einstein to see that.» What does this mean? | It is a sad story about a famous man | It is a rule about maths | You must be a scientist to see it | *It is easy to see
exercise: «Nice one, Einstein!» is said after someone makes an obvious mistake. What does it mean? | *It is sarcastic: the speaker means the person has made a silly mistake | The person has won a prize | Well done, you are very clever | The person is a famous scientist
exercise: Which description fits Albert Einstein best? | *A famous German-born scientist who studied light, time, gravity and energy | A famous singer from Britain | A footballer who scored many goals | A king who lived in a castle
test: Which idea is Albert Einstein known for? | Water boils at 100 degrees | *E = mc² | The Earth goes round the Sun | Pi is about 3.14
test: Jade says Einstein failed maths. What does the text say? | Yes, he failed every test at school | He never went to school | *He did not fail maths; he was very good at it as a boy | He failed maths but was great at art
exam: Which informal word means a very clever person? | *An Einstein | Round the twist | Not the sharpest tool in the shed | A dim-wit
